# Compiled artefacts.
/target/

# Installers and packages produced by packaging/.
/dist/

# Cargo.lock IS committed. This crate produces a binary, and committing the
# lock file is what makes a build reproducible: everyone, including CI and the
# release workflow, compiles the same dependency versions. Libraries leave it
# out so that downstream crates can resolve their own.
# https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html

# Backup files generated by rustfmt.
**/*.rs.bk
